  <diagram name="Page-1" id="CvwjPUeUZ0adulH9_yYM">
    <mxGraphModel dx="337" dy="649" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;what is generics ?&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="210" x="2" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Generics is a feature in java that lets you write a class,method or interface using a placeholder type . so it can work with any data type you choose at the time of use . while the compiler ensures type safety&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="830" x="2" y="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;what is Synchronized ?&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="250" x="2" y="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-4" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Synchronized is a java keyword that puts lock on a method or block so that only one thread can enter it at a time . other thread wait until the lock is released . Synchronized is one way to achieve atomicity&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="830" x="2" y="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-5" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;what is Atomicity ?&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="210" x="2" y="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-6" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Atomicity in java is a concept that ensures an operation completes fully as one indivisible unit . either all steps happen, or none of them happen . no thread can interrupt it in the middle .&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="830" x="2" y="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;what is Stack ?&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="210" x="2" y="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-8" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Stack class in java represents a last in first out (LIFO) stack of objects . it extends class vector with five operations that allow a vector to be treated as a stack . it is thread-safe as all methods are synchronized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;push -&amp;nbsp; Add items to the top&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;pop - Removes and return top item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;peek - Returns top item without removing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;empty - Returns true if stack is empty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;search - Returns position of object from top&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="830" y="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g-vmNKn7EJgvnPABYwxh-9" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Stack&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="90" x="202" y="630" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
